{"requirements":[{"id":"clock-sync-pool","requirement":"Configure node1's system clock to synchronize with pool.ntp.org.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initially unsynchronized chronyd configuration was changed to include `pool pool.ntp.org iburst` and passed chronyd validation. Direct observations then showed NTPSynchronized=yes, Leap status Normal, and a selected source; after reboot, chronyd's current-boot journal explicitly recorded sources selected from pool.ntp.org.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6b17e5e95be446f8","cmd-0c0acbafca9e46fb","cmd-6477076cfaa74480","cmd-1af39641e82a440f","cmd-53e55f21231048c1"]},{"id":"restart-persistence","requirement":"Keep clock synchronization active across restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy synchronized baseline was captured on boot 6001d24d-a752-4a58-a0b2-082876564497, the reboot was acknowledged and connectivity was interrupted, and node1 returned running with boot ID 25163d56-9ba0-4781-8675-ec2f8f6f8fd0. Post-restart evidence showed the pool configuration persisted, chronyd was enabled and active, NTPSynchronized=yes, Leap status Normal, and a selected pool.ntp.org source. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1af39641e82a440f","cmd-d430ee0faf714ce4","cmd-0bc03233822840ff","cmd-7ffe7ef39e5142bd","cmd-8f5f9fe21b91448f","cmd-53e55f21231048c1","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The configuration edit and volatile safety copy supported the requested change; the temporary validation output supported bounded verification and was absent after reboot; enabling/restarting chronyd applied and persisted the configuration; and the scheduled reboot was required both to test persistence and to satisfy the restart protocol. Read-only failed probes caused no evidenced mutations. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, and no new unsafe socket exposure or abnormal temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c0acbafca9e46fb","cmd-6477076cfaa74480","cmd-6bbe71ddb3994cd5","cmd-d430ee0faf714ce4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 directly demonstrated synchronization through pool.ntp.org before reboot and automatic recovery of the persistent configuration and synchronized chronyd service after a verified boot transition. The provider-wide restart evidence protocol is complete for the sole managed node.","limitations":["One post-restart probe attempted to match the selected source against a fresh rotating DNS response and exited unsuccessfully because that response did not contain the already-selected address. The later current-boot chronyd journal directly attributes that selected address to pool.ntp.org, so this limits only the redundant DNS comparison, not the demonstrated outcome (cmd-ffa5133559db492a, cmd-53e55f21231048c1)."]}
